><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250625101911+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250625101913+10'00'" name="08e96c59-7a0c-4d08-82f7-534baeb5b7e4" page="9" coords="36.000000,643.853760,299.021973,643.853760,36.000000,632.823853,299.021973,632.823853,36.000000,632.855713,298.992737,632.855713,36.000000,621.825745,298.992737,621.825745,36.000000,621.857544,299.125580,621.857544,36.000000,610.827637,299.125580,610.827637,36.000000,610.859497,298.944153,610.859497,36.000000,599.829529,298.944153,599.829529,36.000000,599.861328,298.980103,599.861328,36.000000,588.831421,298.980103,588.831421,36.000000,588.863281,299.049133,588.863281,36.000000,577.833313,299.049133,577.833313,36.000000,577.865112,299.016602,577.865112,36.000000,566.835205,299.016602,566.835205,36.000015,566.867065,298.982910,566.867065,36.000015,555.837097,298.982910,555.837097,36.000015,555.868896,299.009003,555.868896,36.000015,544.838989,299.009003,544.838989,36.000015,544.870850,299.027649,544.870850,36.000015,533.840881,299.027649,533.840881,36.000015,533.872681,158.812317,533.872681,36.000015,522.842773,158.812317,522.842773" rect="35.655304,522.498047,299.470276,644.198486" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Ideally, athletes should aim to meet their recommended sleep&#xD;duration in a single nighttime sleep opportunity. In situations&#xD;where this is not possible, athletes can obtain additional sleep&#xD;during a 1- or 2-hour daytime nap opportunity to help meet their&#xD;requirements. In the first hour after waking from a 1- or 2-hour&#xD;daytime nap opportunity, sleep inertia may reduce agility and&#xD;negatively affect aspects of subjective performance—that is,&#xD;athletes may feel sleepy and not ready or motivated to perform.&#xD;Following a long daytime nap opportunity, athletes should&#xD;schedule sufficient time after waking (∼1 h) to ensure they are&#xD;not impaired by sleep inertia.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="9" rect="612.000000,551.853760,796.000000,643.853760"
/></highlight
